{"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "07WM", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-pushouts}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:652bc7d973d09275c2ca36d34fe09b7af41b2716c75d40afb9edf6ac29820409", "source_text": "Pushouts and stacks", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3902e3b6b7e5ff12242b91fb5bf6e478b92df26e779fe12eb3738144e6630120", "unit_id": "tag:07WM:title"}
{"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "07WM", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$Y$", "MATH_0002": "$X'$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$Y'$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:261d6396e74f32459c51fab1cf400aa74a9781ed48e513b90977945a841da1a5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:60c68df8c0c7dcdd7fb4b78624dc4c0d11bf1b6c13dfb2e73be4ec3195d198aa", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we show that algebraic stacks behave well with\nrespect to certain pushouts. The results in this section hold over\nany base scheme.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nThe following lemma is also correct when <MATH_0001>, <MATH_0002>, <MATH_0003>, <MATH_0004> are\nalgebraic spaces, see (insert future reference here).\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:afd5467147f5791a17e7e44820c46da30bfea876e33ab241f43eb786734d70c5", "unit_id": "tag:07WM:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "07WM", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{slogan}\nAlgebraic stacks satisfy the (strong) Rim-Schlessinger condition\n\\end{slogan}", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nX \\ar[r] \\ar[d] & X' \\ar[d] \\\\\nY \\ar[r] & Y'\n}\n$$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$X \\to X'$", "MATH_0005": "$X \\to Y$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0007": "$S$", "MATH_0008": "$$\n\\mathcal{Z}_{Y'}\n\\longrightarrow\n\\mathcal{Z}_Y \\times_{\\mathcal{Z}_X} \\mathcal{Z}_{X'}\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{more-morphisms-lemma-pushout-along-thickening}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-pushout}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ab0008d6ca6d34e8911bb92b071e182fba02ca7aefebb944a3bc37016aa9a5d0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b7e0a81888ea9f995f2235b88d2627a69b923e837ecf621ca76cc90b5bba9726", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let\n<MATH_0002>\nbe a pushout in the category of schemes over <MATH_0003> where <MATH_0004>\nis a thickening and <MATH_0005> is affine, see\nMore on Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nLet <MATH_0006> be an algebraic stack over <MATH_0007>.\nThen the functor of fibre categories\n<MATH_0008>\nis an equivalence of categories.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:539800dcbf161de071f1383543e195f5025628693502d94463012f49d0e649f5", "unit_id": "tag:07WN:statement"}
{"chapter": "artin", "math_text_regions": [{"delimiter_kind": "display-dollar", "pieces": [{"kind": "locked", "placeholder": "MATHSEG_0001"}, {"kind": "text", "slot_id": "math/0001/text/0001"}, {"kind": "locked", "placeholder": "MATHSEG_0002"}], "region_id": "math/0001", "slots": [{"boundary_placeholders": ["MATHSEG_0001", "MATHSEG_0002"], "classification_witness": {"anchor": {"file": "categories.tex", "kind": "section", "matches": [{"command_byte_span": {"end": 242287, "start": 242277}, "command_hash": "sha256:fd3d664c90c8644f5970c6b1608b04e5cf1fc7984e8c9b92c1131eba0cfd124a", "container_byte_span": {"end": 242359, "start": 242149}, "container_hash": "sha256:5e5c65214fc77b4f09f86b1bce6c25714697de4be2e8e78c1a2637d6f027befe"}, {"command_byte_span": {"end": 242783, "start": 242773}, "command_hash": "sha256:fd3d664c90c8644f5970c6b1608b04e5cf1fc7984e8c9b92c1131eba0cfd124a", "container_byte_span": {"end": 242847, "start": 242659}, "container_hash": "sha256:c56690e42ba08b833426b2187a56e6527ac6172fb9b61653b212c3400b48a67f"}, {"command_byte_span": {"end": 243361, "start": 243351}, "command_hash": "sha256:fd3d664c90c8644f5970c6b1608b04e5cf1fc7984e8c9b92c1131eba0cfd124a", "container_byte_span": {"end": 243453, "start": 243199}, "container_hash": "sha256:22bd2849d377c2382ec7d8e17d3577c7f8754022db5b490d58106c1c7300a2de"}], "ordinal": 1, "owner_label": "categories-section-inertia", "owner_tag": "04Z2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14"}, "policy_hash": "sha256:4108cf525225a3a755d96ea80bf1b4fb421350b56ee9543c0b8ab97e2eaa3f9f", "source_label": "categories-section-inertia", "usage": "quad-connector", "usage_source": {"after": "\\quad", "before": "\\quad", "environments": []}}, "command": "text", "policy_entry": "connective-and", "slot_byte_span": {"end": 69, "start": 66}, "slot_id": "math/0001/text/0001", "source": "and"}], "source": "$$\n(\\Sch/Y)_{fppf} \\times_{y, \\mathcal{Z}} \\mathcal{W}\n\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n(\\Sch/X')_{fppf} \\times_{x', \\mathcal{Z}} \\mathcal{W}\n$$", "source_byte_span": {"end": 1186, "start": 1054}, "source_hash": "sha256:dfee4b5d7841f798fc89799c4a5fcc9edd3c81a52fba49e238daa02652934a16"}], "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "07WM", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATHSEG_0001": "$$\n(\\Sch/Y)_{fppf} \\times_{y, \\mathcal{Z}} \\mathcal{W}\n\\quad\\text{", "MATHSEG_0002": "}\\quad\n(\\Sch/X')_{fppf} \\times_{x', \\mathcal{Z}} \\mathcal{W}\n$$", "MATH_0001": "$y'$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathit{Isom}(y', y')$", "MATH_0003": "$Y'$", "MATH_0004": "$I$", "MATH_0005": "$Y'$", "MATH_0006": "$Y'$", "MATH_0007": "$(y, x', f)$", "MATH_0008": "$f : y|_X \\to x'|_X$", "MATH_0009": "$y'$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{Z}_{Y'}$", "MATH_0011": "$Y$", "MATH_0012": "$X'$", "MATH_0013": "$y$", "MATH_0014": "$x'$", "MATH_0015": "$f$", "MATH_0016": "$y'$", "MATH_0017": "$Y'$", "MATH_0018": "$\\mathcal{W}$", "MATH_0019": "$\\mathcal{W} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0020": "$V$", "MATH_0021": "$U'$", "MATH_0022": "$Y$", "MATH_0023": "$X'$", "MATH_0024": "$f$", "MATH_0025": "$\\varphi : V \\times_Y X \\to U' \\times_{X'} X$", "MATH_0026": "$X$", "MATH_0027": "$V' = V \\amalg_{V \\times_Y X} U'$", "MATH_0028": "$Y'$", "MATH_0029": "$Y$", "MATH_0030": "$X'$", "MATH_0031": "$V$", "MATH_0032": "$U'$", "MATH_0033": "$\\varphi$", "MATH_0034": "$W$", "MATH_0035": "$\\mathcal{W}$", "MATH_0036": "$V \\to W$", "MATH_0037": "$U' \\to W$", "MATH_0038": "$V \\times_Y X \\cong U' \\times_{X'} X$", "MATH_0039": "$V' \\to W$", "MATH_0040": "$Y_1'$", "MATH_0041": "$Y_1' \\to V'$", "MATH_0042": "$Y_1 = Y \\times_{Y'} Y_1'$", "MATH_0043": "$X_1' = X' \\times_{Y'} Y_1'$", "MATH_0044": "$X_1 = X \\times_{Y'} Y_1'$", "MATH_0045": "$$\n(\\Sch/Y_1') \\to (\\Sch/V') \\to (\\Sch/W) = \\mathcal{W} \\to \\mathcal{Z}\n$$", "MATH_0046": "$2$", "MATH_0047": "$y_1'$", "MATH_0048": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0049": "$Y_1'$", "MATH_0050": "$Y_1$", "MATH_0051": "$X_1'$", "MATH_0052": "$y|_{Y_1}$", "MATH_0053": "$x'|_{X_1'}$", "MATH_0054": "$f|_{X_1}$", "MATH_0055": "$Y'$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebraic-lemma-representable-diagonal}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-pushouts-lemma-pushout-along-thickening-schemes}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{stacks-lemma-characterize-essentially-surjective-when-ff}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{spaces-pushouts-lemma-pushout-along-thickening}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{spaces-pushouts-lemma-equivalence-categories-spaces-pushout-flat}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0003": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0004": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a91bbd5d9c1f15ff66da6c3ba15d373c36681d0a47ea8c9683d5a833373122d5", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:3555152fac04ead4050982f26052f60b7e669e89079d37dc77881475696fce47", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c3be842d6e044576a9dfed9edab1bfaea9e3ec802a7c57fbe34cd05a2928fe8b", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an object of left hand side. The sheaf\n<MATH_0002> on the category of schemes over <MATH_0003>\nis representable by an algebraic space <MATH_0004> over <MATH_0005>, see\nAlgebraic Stacks, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nWe conclude that the functor of the lemma is fully faithful as\n<MATH_0006> is the pushout in the category of algebraic spaces as\nwell as the category of schemes, see\nPushouts of Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0002>.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nLet <MATH_0007> be an object of the right hand side. Here <MATH_0008>\nis an isomorphism. To finish the proof we have to construct an object <MATH_0009> of\n<MATH_0010> whose restrictions to <MATH_0011> and <MATH_0012> agree with <MATH_0013> and <MATH_0014>\nin a manner compatible with <MATH_0015>. In fact, it suffices to construct <MATH_0016>\nfppf locally on <MATH_0017>, see\nStacks, Lemma <REF_0003>.\nChoose a representable algebraic stack\n<MATH_0018> and a surjective smooth morphism <MATH_0019>.\nThen\n<MATHSEG_0001>and<MATHSEG_0002>\nare algebraic stacks representable by algebraic spaces <MATH_0020> and <MATH_0021>\nsmooth over <MATH_0022> and <MATH_0023>. The isomorphism <MATH_0024> induces an isomorphism\n<MATH_0025> over <MATH_0026>. By\nPushouts of Spaces, Lemmas\n<REF_0004> and\n<REF_0005>\nwe see that the pushout <MATH_0027> is\nan algebraic space smooth over <MATH_0028> whose base change to\n<MATH_0029> and <MATH_0030> recovers <MATH_0031> and <MATH_0032> in a manner compatible with <MATH_0033>.\n\n<STRUCT_0003><STRUCT_0004>\nLet <MATH_0034> be the algebraic space representing <MATH_0035>.\nThe projections <MATH_0036> and <MATH_0037> agree as morphisms\nover <MATH_0038> hence the universal\nproperty of the pushout determines a morphism of algebraic spaces\n<MATH_0039>. Choose a scheme <MATH_0040> and a surjective <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism\n<MATH_0041>. Set <MATH_0042>,\n<MATH_0043>, <MATH_0044>.\nThe composition\n<MATH_0045>\ncorresponds by the <MATH_0046>-Yoneda lemma to an object <MATH_0047> of <MATH_0048>\nover <MATH_0049> whose restriction to <MATH_0050> and <MATH_0051> agrees with <MATH_0052>\nand <MATH_0053> in a manner compatible with <MATH_0054>. Thus we have\nconstructed our desired object smooth locally over <MATH_0055> and we win.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2109d7ac6651d4e9c19738853aa35e0631b57045547c9af9114d41f565683532", "unit_id": "tag:07WN:proof"}
